                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "A very strange game that is very [spoiler]melancholic and heartwrenching.[/spoiler]\r\n\r\nIt's not very long, but that's a good thing for the pacing of the story.\r\n\r\nMisfortune is an endearing character with quite an authentic personality for a child. I'm used to writers portraying kids in a video game as one-dimensional, as being either overly snotty or pleasant. It was amusing to see how accurately Misfortune was written to think about the world and how she reacted to events from a child's point of view.\r\n\r\nThis game quickly caught my interest making me invested in what was to happen. I appreciate when a game can make me feel things that then last in a memorable way.",
